WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.000
Cognitive Load Theory commonly separates load into useful categories.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Intrinsic load comes from the inherent complexity of the material or task.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Some topics have many interacting elements that must be understood together.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.950
Extraneous load comes from the way information is presented when that presentation makes

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.091
learning harder than necessary.

00:00:16.091 --> 00:00:18.000
Germane processing, at a practical level,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.220
is the useful mental effort learners invest in building understanding.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.000
Element interactivity is central to intrinsic load.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
If a task has many parts that depend on each other,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
the learner has to process those relationships together.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.195
For example, learning a single term may be low in element interactivity.

00:00:33.195 --> 00:00:36.915
Learning a process where timing, roles, conditions, and exceptions interact is higher.

00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:40.110
Designers cannot remove all intrinsic load without changing the task,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.995
but they can manage how much complexity appears at once.

00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:44.970
Extraneous load is the avoidable burden.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.000
It appears when slides are cluttered, labels are unclear,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.000
diagrams are separated from explanations, navigation is confusing, examples are weak,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
or narration fights with on-screen text.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Learners may spend effort locating information, reconciling duplicate explanations,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
or ignoring decorative material instead of understanding the core idea.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.000
That effort feels like learning work, but it does not help much.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.915
The practical distinction is productive mental effort versus wasted mental effort.

00:01:08.915 --> 00:01:12.915
Productive effort helps learners connect ideas, form schemas, and prepare for performance.

00:01:12.915 --> 00:01:14.970
Wasted effort is friction created by the instruction.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.915
Good design cannot make every topic easy, and it should not remove all challenge.

00:01:18.915 --> 00:01:23.250
But it can protect learner attention by reducing unnecessary difficulty and directing

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.960
effort toward understanding.
